<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 4 Best in Slot Gear list for Feral Druid DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Icecrown Citadel and Ruby Sanctum on 25-man Heroic difficulty, with listed alternatives from the 10-man and Normal difficulty versions of the raids as well. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Feral Druid DPS Phase 4</h2>Just as in Phase 1-3, Item Level remains the single most impactful attribute on any piece of gear in Phase 4, as it directly determines the total allocation of useful DPS stats on each item. This means that you can continue to use Item Level as an excellent proxy for DPS value when evaluating potential upgrades for your Feral Druid in Phase 4. Depending on the gear slot, the highest Item Level that is attainable from Phase 4 raid drops is either 277 (from 25-man Heroic difficulty bosses in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>) or 284 (from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=39863/halion">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Halion</span></a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36597/the-lich-king">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Lich King</span></a>), and unsurprisingly, the embedded full BiS setup below uses a 277 or 284 Item Level piece in every slot where one is available.<br/>
<br/>The main scenario where deviating from maximum Item Level is optimal for Phase 4 gearing is when itemizing for the 4-piece <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-845/lasherweave-battlegear">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Lasherweave Battlegear</span></a> Tier 10 set bonus, which is so overpowered for cat DPS that completing the set takes priority over any other gearing considerations. In fact, simulation comparisons conclusively show that even the base version of the Tier 10 set, which is only 251 Item Level and where every piece individually is worse than even <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/dps-bis-gear-pve-phase-3">Phase 3 BiS gear</a>, is worth using over the best 264 Item Level off-piece options from 10-man Heroic or 25-man Normal ICC, simply due to the power of the bonus. Even in Phase 3 gear, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48574/rake">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_disembowel.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rake</span></a> accounts for almost 8% of a cat's total single target DPS output, so it is unsurprising that allowing the ability's periodic damage (which is already the dominant component) to Crit provides enormous DPS gains. This is especially true at late ICC gear levels, where Ferals can expect around 74% of their special abilities to Crit against boss targets in a raid environment, and where the 4-piece bonus will provide around 750 DPS of value (in addition to the stats on the Tier pieces themselves).<br/>
<br/>The only other change from Phase 3 gearing priorities is that both intermediate and full BiS ICC gear setups will optimally stack Armor Penetration Rating all the way up to the stat's hard cap of 1399. This is because both new BiS physical DPS trinkets introduced in Phase 4, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54590/sharpened-twilight-scale">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubysanctum4.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sharpened Twilight Scale</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50363/deathbringers-will">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deathbringer's Will</span></a>, significantly out-perform <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45931/mjolnir-runestone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rune_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mjolnir Runestone</span></a> from Phase 2-3. As a result, you will no longer need to worry about staying below the Armor Penetration soft cap of 648 Rating, and will always benefit from more passive Armor Penetration Rating on your gear or gems, until you reach the hard cap. Furthermore, at ICC gear levels, Armor Penetration also scales harder than any other melee DPS stat besides Hit or Expertise because it exhibits <i>increasing returns</i>, meaning that the stat becomes more and more valuable as you accumulate high levels of it passively on your gear. This unique scaling behavior arises from the nonlinear formula used for computing enemy damage mitigation in Classic WoW, and makes hard stacking <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40117/fractured-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Cardinal Ruby</span></a> gems (even ignoring socket bonuses to do so) optimal as soon you replace <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45931/mjolnir-runestone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rune_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mjolnir Runestone</span></a>.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="25-man">25-Man BiS</h3>With the above gearing priorities in mind, shown below is the absolute highest DPS gear configuration that can be assembled by a Feral Druid in Phase 4:<br/>
