<div class="gear-planner-slots-controls">
<div class="gear-planner-slots-controls-buttons">
<a class="btn btn-small gear-planner-button-container-link fa fa-link" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/gear-planner/druid/tauren/BgBQFfUjICEyMiASBTEgAwMQUR8gNQMBLx8wMGNtNjcxMXhqZjIxbmd6MzFyZzE0MXN0azUxcmZ6gUDIYADqMgChtiCctQIgxckAnLWDIMhjAOoeAJy1hUDIYgDtFACctSCcvQZgxhMAnLUgnLVAnLaHQMhhAOymAJywIJy9iEDFrwDW6ACcvSCc1Ikg1TQArh8AnLWKQMXzANbXAJy9IJy1CyDVMACc1AwgxawAnNQNANU-DgDEu48gxd0A1toAnL2QYMYvAOjlAJywIL_WQJzUEgDFGA" style="margin-left:5px;float:right">Link</a>
<button class="btn btn-small fa fa-user gear-planner-button-container-model">Toggle Model</button></div>
<div class="slider not-editable has-labels" data-track="progress">
<div class="slider-track">
<div class="slider-track-handle" style="left: 100%;"></div>
<div class="slider-track-bar">
<div class="slider-track-bar-progress" style="width: 100%;"></div></div></div>
<div class="slider-labels">
<span class="slider-labels-title">Level</span>
<span class="slider-labels-values">
<span class="slider-labels-values-sizer">80</span>
<input class="slider-labels-values-input" data-field-filled="true" disabled="" style="width: 20px;" type="text"/>
<span class="slider-labels-values-max">80</span></span></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<br/>When using a <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42995/hearty-rhino">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_food_115_condorsoup.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hearty Rhino</span></a> food buff, the combination of gear pieces and gems in this setup results in a total Armor Penetration Rating value of 1395, which is just shy of the cap without exceeding it, making it more efficient than alternative 4pT10 setups with different off-piece combinations.<br/>
<br/>Note that the BiS setup includes the Engineering-exclusive enchants <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=54999/hyperspeed-accelerators">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hyperspeed Accelerators</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55002/flexweave-underlay">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flexweave Underlay</span></a>. As mentioned in our <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/dps-overview-pve#best-professions">class overview guide</a>, <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=202/engineering">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> is such an insanely overpowered profession for PvE that it is assumed that any competitive Feral DPS player will have it. In contrast, your second profession choice has hardly any impact in WotLK since all crafting professions provide very comparable PvE benefits, so no other profession-exclusive gear augmentations are assumed.<br/>
<br/>Also note that the displayed configuration is optimized for <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_horde.gif");'></span>
<span class="q10">Horde</span> players, but the BiS gear pieces are identical for both factions. If you are an <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_alliance.gif");'></span>
<span class="q3">Alliance</span> Feral and are lucky enough to have a <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="race" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/draenei">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_male.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Draenei</span></a> in your party providing the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=6562/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a> buff, then simply swap out three of the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40125/rigid-kings-amber">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_38.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid King's Amber</span></a> gems for <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40143/etched-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Etched Ametrine</span></a> gems instead, in order to stay below your reduced Hit cap of 7%.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="10-man">10-Man BiS</h3>Several of the 25-man Heroic bosses in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a> are <i>considerably</i> more challenging than any prior raid content in Classic WoW, including both <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4075/sunwell-plateau">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sunwell Plateau</span></a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> Hard Modes. As a result, many of the items in the above full BiS setup may be inaccessible to you for several weeks or months while your raid team is still learning the Heroic encounters. For this reason, a separate 10-man BiS setup is presented just below as an intermediate stepping stone between Phase 3 gear and full Phase 4 BiS. This configuration includes only items obtainable from either 10-man Heroic ICC and Ruby Sanctum encounters (which are much easier than their 25-man counterparts) or from prior phase 25-man content:<br/>
