<br/>Notice that this intermediate setup is not limited by the Armor Penetration hard cap of 1399 Rating, and therefore exclusively gems <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40117/fractured-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Cardinal Ruby</span></a> after capping Hit and Expertise. Furthermore, since the setup does not exceed 1279 Armor Penetration Rating even with a <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42995/hearty-rhino">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_food_115_condorsoup.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hearty Rhino</span></a> food buff, simulations have shown that it is optimal to use the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=42976/executioner">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_2h_auchindoun_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Executioner</span></a> weapon enchant from TBC in place of the Berserking enchant that is normally recommended. Once you obtain enough 25-man ICC upgrades to raise your passive Armor Penetration Rating to above 1279 (the "Executioner soft cap"), then swapping back to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=59621/enchant-weapon-berserking">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulasuperior_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Weapon - Berserking</span></a> will provide higher DPS.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="ruby-sanctum">Updates for Best in Slot Gear in Ruby Sanctum</h3>The new Ruby Sanctum raid drops only a small handful of items relevant to Feral Druids: <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54590/sharpened-twilight-scale">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubysanctum4.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sharpened Twilight Scale</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54580/umbrage-armbands">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_41.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Umbrage Armbands</span></a>, and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54576/signet-of-twilight">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_icecrownringc.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signet of Twilight</span></a>. Of these, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54590/sharpened-twilight-scale">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubysanctum4.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sharpened Twilight Scale</span></a> is by far the most important upgrade to prioritize, as it provides a hefty 270 DPS increase over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50343/whispering-fanged-skull">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Whispering Fanged Skull</span></a> from 10-man ICC. However, if you are already decked out in near-BiS ICC gear (including <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50363/deathbringers-will">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deathbringer's Will</span></a>), then simply swapping in <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54590/sharpened-twilight-scale">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubysanctum4.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sharpened Twilight Scale</span></a> will put you far above the Armor Penetration hard cap of 1399 Rating. As a result, in order to maximize the value of the new trinket, a number of complementary itemization changes were made in the full BiS 25-man setup shown earlier in the guide:<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<img alt="" class="no-border" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/icons/horde.png"/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47546/sylvanas-cunning">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_18.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sylvanas' Cunning</span></a> /<wbr/> <img alt="" class="no-border" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/guide/images/27798.png"/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47545/vereesas-dexterity">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vereesa's Dexterity</span></a> was swapped out in favor of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50653/shadowvault-slayers-cloak">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_icecrowncloak.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shadowvault Slayer's Cloak</span></a> in order to drop some Armor Penetration Rating.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54580/umbrage-armbands">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_41.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Umbrage Armbands</span></a>, also off <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=39863/halion">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Halion</span></a> on 25-man Heroic difficulty, were used over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50670/toskks-maximized-wristguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_41.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Toskk's Maximized Wristguards</span></a> as an additional Armor Penetration drop.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Finally, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40117/fractured-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Cardinal Ruby</span></a> gems were substituted with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40118/precise-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precise Cardinal Ruby</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40112/delicate-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Delicate Cardinal Ruby</span></a> gems one by one until the gear set dropped to below the Armor Penetration cap.</div></li></ul>Note that a secondary consequence of dropping <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50343/whispering-fanged-skull">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Whispering Fanged Skull</span></a> is that it is now possible to stay below the Crit soft cap, which is 77.66% raid buffed Crit chance when using <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50456/idol-of-the-crying-moon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_natureguardian.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Crying Moon</span></a>. As a result, players who are lucky enough to possess both <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54590/sharpened-twilight-scale">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubysanctum4.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sharpened Twilight Scale</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50363/deathbringers-will">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deathbringer's Will</span></a> can swap back to socketing mostly Agility gems rather than Strength gems after capping out on Armor Penetration Rating.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Frost for Feral Druid DPS Phase 4</h3>As mentioned at the start of this guide, the most important gearing priority for Feral Druids at the start of Phase 4 will be completing the 4-piece <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-845/lasherweave-battlegear">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Lasherweave Battlegear</span></a> set bonus, so all of your initial <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> accumulation during the first month of the phase should go towards 251 Item Level Tier 10 pieces. Note that unlike the Tier 9 set in Phase 3, purchasing these base pieces from Emblems is a <i>prerequisite</i> to obtaining the upgraded 264 or 277 Item Level versions of each item from raid token drops, making it even more important to purchase all four pieces of 251 Tier as soon as possible. Since the 264 Item Level upgrade token (<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a>) drops from both 10-man Heroic and 25-man Normal ICC, you may easily find yourself in a scenario where you already have some of these tokens sitting in your bags, but cannot use them until you obtain more Emblems.<br/>
<br/>The optimal four pieces of Tier 10 to target for cat DPS early on in the phase are the helm, chest, glove, and leg slots. This is because the shoulder slot has the strongest available off-piece option across the five slots for early ICC gear progression, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51830/skinned-whelp-shoulders">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shoulder_112.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skinned Whelp Shoulders</span></a>, which are also quite accessible since they are a 10-man drop. Even if you have no ICC off-pieces to choose from and are slotting the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-845/lasherweave-battlegear">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Lasherweave Battlegear</span></a> set into a Phase 3 setup, using <img alt="" class="no-border" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/icons/horde.png"/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48198/runetotems-shoulderpads-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shoulder_109b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Runetotem's Shoulderpads of Triumph</span></a> /<wbr/> <img alt="" class="no-border" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/guide/images/27798.png"/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48207/malfurions-shoulderpads-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shoulder_89.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Malfurion's Shoulderpads of Triumph</span></a> as your off-piece will still outperform alternative 4pT10 configurations. Note that full Phase 4 BiS setups will opt to use the glove slot as an off-piece instead, but this is only correct once you are decked out in 277 Item Level Heroic loot and your itemization is constrained by the Armor Penetration hard cap.<br/>
<br/>Among these four Tier 10 slots, it is worth targeting <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50827/lasherweave-handgrips">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_83.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lasherweave Handgrips</span></a> as your first <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> purchase if you anticipate obtaining a <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> early on, since the 264 Item Level version of the gloves will be the largest individual upgrade from the Phase 3 BiS option in that slot (<img alt="" class="no-border" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/guide/images/27798.png"/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47945/gloves-of-the-silver-assassin">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_77a.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gloves of the Silver Assassin</span></a> /<wbr/> <img alt="" class="no-border" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/icons/horde.png"/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48202/runetotems-handgrips-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_78b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Runetotem's Handgrips of Triumph</span></a>). The next Tier slot to target if you anticipate early <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> priority is the leg slot, since <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51142/sanctified-lasherweave-legguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_35.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sanctified Lasherweave Legguards</span></a> are also individually an appreciable upgrade over <img alt="" class="no-border" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/guide/images/27798.png"/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48205/malfurions-legguards-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Malfurion's Legguards of Triumph</span></a> /<wbr/> <img alt="" class="no-border" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/icons/horde.png"/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45536/legguards-of-cunning-deception">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Legguards of Cunning Deception</span></a> from Phase 3. The helm and chest pieces on the other hand are at best sidegrades from Phase 3 alternatives even when upgraded using <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a>, and should only be equipped once you obtain all four pieces in order to activate the set bonus.<br/>
<br/>Once you have obtained all four Tier 10 pieces, the only remaining <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> reward in the full BiS setup above is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50456/idol-of-the-crying-moon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_natureguardian.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Crying Moon</span></a>, which is unfortunately a minuscule upgrade over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47668/idol-of-mutilation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of Mutilation</span></a> from Phase 3, and can even be a downgrade on encounters with periods of melee downtime, due to the ramp-up time for building up <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71175/agile">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_druid_feralchargecat.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Agile</span></a> stacks. The other rewards are all outclassed by 277 Item Level drops from 25-man Heroic ICC bosses, but can serve as solid intermediate upgrades while you are waiting for the BiS option to drop. In particular, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50995/vengeful-noose">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_noose_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vengeful Noose</span></a> provides a hefty DPS increase over <img alt="" class="no-border" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/icons/horde.png"/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47460/belt-of-the-pitiless-killer">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_38b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Belt of the Pitiless Killer</span></a> /<wbr/> <img alt="" class="no-border" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/guide/images/27798.png"/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47112/belt-of-the-merciless-killer">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_37c.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Belt of the Merciless Killer</span></a> from Phase 3, and is worth prioritizing over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50456/idol-of-the-crying-moon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_natureguardian.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Crying Moon</span></a> unless you get lucky with an early <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50707/astrylians-sutured-cinch">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_61.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Astrylian's Sutured Cinch</span></a> drop.<br/>
<br/>
