<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="rings">Rings for Feral Druid DPS Phase 4</h3>With the release of <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4987/the-ruby-sanctum">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Ruby Sanctum</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54576/signet-of-twilight">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_icecrownringc.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signet of Twilight</span></a> becomes the new highest DPS ring for Feral Druids in Phase 4, since it is the only 284 Item Level option available in the slot.<br/>
<br/>The second ring slot is much more flexible by comparison, and the optimal choice will vary depending on the rest of your gear. In full BiS setups, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50604/band-of-the-bone-colossus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_83.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of the Bone Colossus</span></a> is used because all of the Hit Rating on it can be efficiently accommodated without exceeding the cap, and because full BiS configurations are limited by the Armor Penetration hard cap even without running any passive Armor Penetration Rating in either ring slot. When wearing full Ruby Sanctum gear, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50604/band-of-the-bone-colossus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_83.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of the Bone Colossus</span></a> also outperforms the previously BiS ring <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50402/ashen-band-of-endless-vengeance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_81.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ashen Band of Endless Vengeance</span></a>, since its lack of Critical Strike Rating allows optimized gear sets to stay below the Crit soft cap (77.66% raid buffed Crit chance with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50456/idol-of-the-crying-moon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_natureguardian.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Crying Moon</span></a>) even when socketing <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40112/delicate-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Delicate Cardinal Ruby</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40148/glinting-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glinting Ametrine</span></a> gems. However, for earlier gear progression on a fresh character, where you will be far below the Armor Penetration cap and are still running pieces like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47077/treads-of-the-icewalker">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_leather_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Treads of the Icewalker</span></a> with a high Hit Rating allocation, then <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50618/frostbrood-sapphire-ring">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_icecrownringa.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frostbrood Sapphire Ring</span></a> will provide significantly more DPS than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50604/band-of-the-bone-colossus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_83.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of the Bone Colossus</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Ring Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=44645/enchant-ring-assault">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Ring - Assault</span></a>, requires <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=333/enchanting">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchanting</span></a>. <br/>Only Enchanters may apply ring enchants on their own rings.<div class="pad"></div>
<table class="grid max-width">
<tbody>
<tr>
