<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="trinkets">Trinkets for Feral Druid DPS Phase 4</h3>The absolute best DPS trinket for Feral Druids in Phase 4 of WotLK continues to be the highly coveted <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50363/deathbringers-will">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deathbringer's Will</span></a>. This trinket singlehandedly allows any ICC-geared Feral to reach the Armor Penetration cap without the use of the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=42976/executioner">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_2h_auchindoun_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Executioner</span></a> weapon enchant, making it scale extraordinarily well due to the increasing returns of Armor Penetration Rating. On top of this, the trinket randomly provides one of three high value procs for Druids: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71561/strength-of-the-taunka">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_character_tauren_male.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Strength of the Taunka</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71556/agility-of-the-vrykul">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_kingymiron_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Agility of the Vrykul</span></a>, or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71560/speed-of-the-vrykul">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_kingymiron_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Speed of the Vrykul</span></a>. Simulation comparisons indicate that the Heroic version of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50363/deathbringers-will">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deathbringer's Will</span></a> provides a whopping 400-500 DPS increase for Ferals over the Phase 3 BiS trinket <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47131/deaths-verdict">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death's Verdict</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47464/deaths-choice">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death's Choice</span></a>, depending on the player's gear level, and even the Normal version will vastly outclass any alternative options from ICC or prior raids.<br/>
<br/>However, the new Ruby Sanctum raid brings with it <i>another</i> highly coveted Armor Penetration trinket, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54590/sharpened-twilight-scale">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubysanctum4.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sharpened Twilight Scale</span></a>, which is nearly as strong as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50363/deathbringers-will">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deathbringer's Will</span></a> and provides a hefty 270 DPS upgrade over the previous BiS option <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50343/whispering-fanged-skull">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Whispering Fanged Skull</span></a>. As a result, using both <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50363/deathbringers-will">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deathbringer's Will</span></a> + <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54590/sharpened-twilight-scale">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubysanctum4.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sharpened Twilight Scale</span></a> together is the optimal trinket pairing in endgame BiS setups for players who are fortunate enough to obtain both. Note that in order to maximize the value of this trinket pairing, you will need to re-itemize the rest of your gear set to stay below the Armor Penetration hard cap of 1399 Rating, as described <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/dps-bis-gear-pve-phase-4#ruby-sanctum">earlier</a> in this guide.<br/>
<br/>Finally, for players who are in the process of gearing up new Ferals, it should be noted that <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45931/mjolnir-runestone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rune_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mjolnir Runestone</span></a>, which was the top DPS trinket for Ferals in Phase 2-3, will be replaced almost immediately once you have access to Phase 4 loot. This is because Phase 4 gear upgrades (including BoE crafted gear, <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> rewards, and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a> raid drops) are itemized with so much passive Armor Penetration that you will start exceeding the soft cap of 648 Rating with just a handful of upgrades,  making the trinket's proc far less valuable. Furthermore, the easy availability of both Normal <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47115/deaths-verdict">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death's Verdict</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45609/comets-trail">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_arcane_starfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Comet's Trail</span></a> from the <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=2711/defilers-scourgestone">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Defiler's Scourgestone</span></span></a> vendor means that it will quickly become optimal to drop <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45931/mjolnir-runestone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rune_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mjolnir Runestone</span></a> and stack passive Armor Penetration on the rest of your gear instead.<div class="pad"></div>
